==Strategy==
This stage may seem much more difficult due to the inability to use cats such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] or even the ability to cheese it with [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]], but If you have [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], the same Stone stalling strategy applies here.

Attack and meatshield using [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], then use [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to deal with the peons.

Usage of [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] is not recommended (Unless if paired up with a specific Uber Rare Cat,) as they can make Kappy activate surges, unlike Macho Crystal Cat.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Just like the original stage, you have to try and make Kappy Jr. miss constantly by using the Scissoroos or knocking him back. Some useful Ubers for this stage include: all [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST Ubers]] and units like [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] and [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]]. It's recommended you don't bring Ubers with Crowd-Control abilities anyways though, since they may alter your [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]'s timing.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: He works here just as well as in the original stage, just be aware he might die quickly. He can also deal chip damage to the Scisscoroos.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Myrcia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Myrcia ξ]]: With Surge Immunity, Myrcia can safely chip down Kappy while simultaneously killing swathes of minor peons using her Waves. Keep an eye on the Scissoroos though, as she'll be gone in a blink if they find an opening to her.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]]: With support from [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist]] and [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], you can subdue Kappy Jr. quite easily, not to mention alien targeting as well to keep the Scissoroos in check. Do watch out for any potential surges and you may not even need Boulder Cat.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: As long as he is supported with Macho Crystal and proper Rock timings to ensure you keep him alive for a while, he'll dispose of nearly every enemy here including Kappy himself. There is a high chance Cosmo will die mid-fight so you should stall the enemies until you spawn another Cosmo, then rinse and repeat.

